Subject: [parser] Preserve strict arrow parameter errors across nested parens

In ExpressionScope::RecordStrictModeParameterError, when already in
strict mode, record the declaration error directly on the current
ArrowHeadParsingScope rather than storing it in
next_arrow_function_info_.strict_parameter_error_location. Previously,
when an arrow parameter like 'eval' or 'arguments' in strict mode was
followed by a parenthesized expression or call in a default initializer
(e.g. '(eval, a = (1)) => eval'), the inner ArrowHeadParsingScope cleared
next_arrow_function_info_ and lost the outer arrow parameter error.

Bug: 567222737
